status: parked
goal: Build position aggregation layer for live trading — virtual positions per strategy, net execution on exchange, reconciliation
priority: DEFERRED — tackle when ready to move from paper to real capital
started: 2026-03-14
type: infrastructure

trigger: |
  Paper trading runs 21 pools with multiple strategies trading the same tokens.
  Multiple strategies can hold positions in the same token simultaneously.
  In paper trading these are independent virtual positions — correct and matching
  institutional best practices. But when going live on Binance, the exchange sees
  a single net position per token. Need an aggregation layer between virtual books
  and exchange execution.

architecture: |

  === CURRENT STATE (paper trading — correct) ===

  v4/position.py PositionManager tracks per-strategy virtual positions.
  Each Position has strategy_id, direction, quantity, margin, funding.
  Multiple strategies can hold the same token independently.
  This IS the institutional "virtual position book" pattern.

  === TARGET STATE (live trading) ===

  Strategy A: virtual +2 BTC  ──┐
  Strategy B: virtual -0.5 BTC ─┤── Aggregation Layer ── Exchange: +1.5 BTC
  Strategy C: virtual +0.3 BTC ─┘

  Virtual positions (strategy-level) → Net position (exchange-level)
  Delta execution: only trade the difference between desired net and current exchange position.

  === BINANCE SPECIFICS ===

  Use ONE-WAY MODE (not Hedge Mode). Reasons:
  - Hedge Mode only gives 2 slots (long+short), doesn't help with 3+ strategies same direction
  - Hedge Mode doubles margin (gross vs net) and doubles funding costs
  - All institutional firms use virtual books + net execution in one-way mode

  Consider PORTFOLIO MARGIN when going live:
  - 350+ collateral assets, cross-product PnL offset
  - Unified maintenance margin ratio (uniMMR)
  - Significantly reduces capital requirements for hedged portfolios

implementation_phases: |

  PHASE 1: Net Position Dashboard (LOW effort, do during paper trading)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Add NetPositionTracker alongside existing PositionManager.
  For each token: sum all virtual positions → show net on dashboard.
  Show margin-with-netting vs gross margin (capital planning metric).
  No execution changes — pure visibility.

  PHASE 2: Position Aggregation Layer (MEDIUM effort, pre-live)
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  PositionAggregator sits between virtual books and exchange API.
  - compute_desired_net(token) → sum of virtual positions
  - compute_delta(token, exchange_position) → order to send
  - allocate_fill(fill, strategies) → proportional attribution
  - reconcile(token, exchange_position) → alert on mismatch

  PHASE 3: Order Management (HIGH effort, for live)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Full order lifecycle: place → partial fill → complete → allocate.
  Partial fill handling: keep strategy position "partially closed" until full exit.
  Liquidation propagation: detect exchange liquidation → allocate loss proportionally.
  Consider NautilusTrader or Talos as alternatives to building from scratch.

key_challenges: |

  C1. FUNDING RATE ALLOCATION
      Each strategy's funding = funding_rate × virtual_qty × mark_price.
      Sum of strategy-level funding == exchange-level funding. Mathematically exact.
      Current v4/position.py cumulative_funding tracking is already correct.

  C2. MARGIN NETTING BENEFIT
      Net position margin < sum of gross position margins.
      Paper trading is CONSERVATIVE on margin — live will use ~40% less in hedged cases.
      Good problem to have (paper results understate capital efficiency).

  C3. PARTIAL FILLS
      Strategy A exits → sell order partially fills → virtual position is
      "partially closed" until remainder fills. Must track fill allocation.
      This is the hardest operational problem.

  C4. LIQUIDATION PROPAGATION
      Net position liquidated → ALL strategies with positions in that token affected.
      Must allocate liquidation loss proportionally across contributing strategies.
      Set liquidation buffers at aggregation layer level, not strategy level.

  C5. ONE STRATEGY'S EXIT FLIPPING NET DIRECTION
      Strategy A long +2, Strategy B short -0.5. Net = +1.5.
      Strategy A exits → net = -0.5. Exchange must sell 2.0 to go from +1.5 to -0.5.
      Aggregation layer handles this naturally via delta computation.

references: |

  Industry pattern: Jump, Wintermute, Cumberland/DRW, Millennium, Citadel all use
  virtual position books + net execution. This is the "pod model" from TradFi multi-
  strategy hedge funds (Aurum, CAIS research).

  Binance docs:
  - Hedge Mode: binance.com/en/support/faq/360041513552
  - Portfolio Margin: binance.com/en/portfolio-margin
  - Multi-Assets Mode: binance.com/en/blog/futures/multiassets-mode
